# Tailwind CSS Rules

## Class Organization
- Use consistent class ordering
- Group related classes together
- Use responsive prefixes consistently
- Prefer utility classes over custom CSS

## Responsive Design
- Mobile-first approach
- Use proper breakpoints (sm, md, lg, xl, 2xl)
- Test on multiple screen sizes
- Use proper spacing and typography scales

```tsx
// ✅ Good Tailwind usage
<div className="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 p-6 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg shadow-md">
  <h2 className="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
    Blog Post Title
  </h2>
  <p className="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
    Post content here
  </p>
</div>
```

## Dark Mode
- Use dark: prefix for dark mode styles
- Test both light and dark themes
- Use CSS variables for consistent theming
- Implement proper color contrast

## Component Consistency
- Use consistent spacing (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32)
- Use consistent border radius
- Use consistent shadow styles
- Create reusable component patterns